id-empire","cpn":"Achaemenid Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wars_of_Alexander_the_Great","c":3},{"y":-326,"t":"gain","x":"327-326: the Assakenoi and Aspasioi.","m":4,"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wars_of_Alexander_the_Great","c":2},{"y":-326,"t":"gain","x":"May 326: the Hydaspes.","m":5,"cp":"Porus and the Indian kingdoms of the Punjab","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wars_of_Alexander_the_Great","c":3},{"y":-325,"t":"vassal_end","x":"c. 325: Seuthes III revolts. 'Seuthes revolted against Macedon in about 325 BC, after Alexander's governor' (Zopyrion) was beaten by the Getae; the Odrysian kingdom page has the rebellion 'at the end of the 330s or in the mid-320s (the dating is not entirely clear)'.","cp":"odrysian-kingdom","cpn":"Odrysian Kingdom","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seuthes_III","c":2},{"y":-325,"t":"loss","x":"c. 325: Seuthes III's realm around Seuthopolis passes out of Macedonian hands. Same region as odrysian-kingdom's c. 325 gain; Seuthes 'ruled only part of Thrace', the coast staying with the Macedonian strategoi (and later Lysimachus).","cp":"odrysian-kingdom","cpn":"Odrysian Kingdom","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seuthes_III","c":2},{"y":-323,"t":"vassal_end","x":"323: the Lamian War breaks the League of Corinth.","cp":"greek-city-states","cpn":"Greek city-states (independent poleis)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lamian_War","c":2},{"y":-323,"t":"contest_start","x":"323-322: the Lamian War's fighting zone (rule 6 blend).","cp":"athenian-coalition","cpn":"Hellenic League of the Lamian War","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lamian_War","c":3},{"y":-323,"t":"vassal_start","x":"June 323: the Partition of Babylon.","m":6,"cp":"kingdom-of-lysimachus","cpn":"Kingdom of Lysimachus","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Partition_of_Babylon","c":3},{"y":-323,"t":"vassal_start","x":"June 323: Syria to Laomedon (Partition of Babylon; confirmed at Triparadisus 321).","m":6,"cp":"laomedon","cpn":"Laomedon of Mytilene (satrapy of